---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site, url } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  'Terms for using Lina. Hotel rates and availability belong to the booking site. Lina is an editorial list, not the merchant.';
---

<Base title="Terms" description={description}>
  <article class="wrap page-hero">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Terms' }]} />
    <p class="kicker">Updated 23 October 2026</p>
    <h1>How to read this site.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Lina is operated by {site.operator}. The pages are general information about hotels and about how to look for
        one. They are not an offer of accommodation, and Lina is not the merchant. A booking is a contract between you
        and Booking.com or the hotel, on their terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Prices, availability, taxes, and cancellation rules change. When Lina prints a rate, the page will say the
        date it was checked, the room, and the occupancy. Most entries currently say TODO instead of a number, because
        a rate has not been checked. Do not treat a missing number, a neighborhood description, or an older article as
        the price you will pay. Read the booking page before you pay.
      </p>
      <p>
        Facts on a hotel page are kept short on purpose, and they can still go stale. Official star categories are
        repeated only when the hotel states them, and they are not guest scores. Photographs of cities are stock
        images with credits. They are not photographs of the hotels.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some links are affiliate links, described in the <a href={url('/disclosure')}>affiliate disclosure</a>. A
        commission does not raise your rate. It also does not make Lina responsible for the stay.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, Lina and its operator are not liable for a rate
        that changed, a room that differed from a listing, or a trip decision you made from these pages. Nothing here
        limits liability that cannot legally be limited.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. See also the
        <a href={url('/privacy')}>privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
